WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.480
I can too wake up early if I feel like it!

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:15.620
It looks like the Principal isn't here yet.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.000
Once a Day

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.000
Let's keep this our little secret.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:38.530
Miss Yoshinoya, I'm very sorry for how angry I've gotten in the past.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:44.020
From now on, feel free to come in as late as you'd like.

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.560
One, two, three, four!

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.210
Two, two, three, four!

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.540
Three, two, three, four!

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:10.570
Four...

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.170
Morning. You sure are getting into it.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:16.800
Miya! Do you want to try it too?

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.050
Sure, it looks fun.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.510
One, two, three, four!

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:26.110
Two, two, three, four!

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:29.190
Yuno, Miya...

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:33.690
Sorry, did we wake you up?

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:37.040
You've got to smile brighter.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.700
If you don't smile, you'll get points taken off.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.450
She must still be asleep.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:49.460
April 15th

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:49.460
Satisfying
Sunlight

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.460
Art Dept.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.820
That's it for today!

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:58.150
The teachers have an inservice this afternoon.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.380
What are you going to do when we get home?

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:04.390
I'm going to eat lunch, then I'll think about it.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.130
Wanna go to the cafeteria?

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.140
Sure.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.060
Wow, I wonder if we'll be able to find somewhere to sit.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.160
Let's buy lunch first.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.150
Oh, Yuno, Miyako!

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:20.150
Meal Tickets

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.060
Nori, you're here too.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.490
So, you got katsudon?

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.660
We're going to go get something now. Want to sit together?

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.670
I'm eating with some kids from my class. I had them save me a seat.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.010
Oh.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.170
What's Nazuna doing?

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:41.550
Dunno. I haven't seen her at school today.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.930
I see.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:44.640
Over here!

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.030
Anyway, later.

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:47.840
Sure.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.800
Did Nazuna go home early?

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:53.850
I guess.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.740
Sae... Huh?

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.450
She's alone?

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.180
Go for it, Natsume!

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.450
Do your best.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:11.540
Why?

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.550
It's rare to see you walking home by yourself.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:26.970
Did something happen?

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:30.100
Nah, I just forgot something in the classroom.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.230
Going back and getting it took me a while.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:35.230
Well, that's nice.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:37.480
What do you mean by that?

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.630
How's your class doing? Is everything going fine?

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:46.530
How it's doing? Same as always, really. Still the same people.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.710
Yeah, I guess.

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.200
All right, I'm here.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:52.290
Thanks.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:00.050
For walking home with me.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.840
It just ended up that way!

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.360
Anyway, see you tomorrow!

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:11.850
Sae!

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:17.100
I'm all ready to go!

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.980
Ah, sorry.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:29.410
Hi. Thanks for before.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.240
What is it, Nori?

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.710
Well, I'd like to get some curtains.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.210
You know anywhere around here that sells them?

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:41.100
Curtains? I know I've seen them somewhere.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.020
Sae and Hiro already went out, right?

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:44.800
Yeah.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.050
Oh, maybe Nazuna knows.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.680
That's right, Nazuna is a townie.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:53.220
A townie?

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:54.810
An Italian?

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.310
Curtains?

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.310
Yeah, you know somewhere that has them?

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:05.360
I'm Home probably would.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.040
I'm Home?

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:09.950
Um, it's kind of like a hardware store.

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.490
Do they sell lots of things?

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:14.700
Yeah, they have plenty of things,

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:19.960
like frying pans, trash bags, shelves, screws, planters...

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.290
...and gnomes.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:22.960
Gnomes!?

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:25.440
Sorry to drag you along.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:26.580
No problem.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.470
It's kind of hard to explain where it is.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.760
Hey, mind if we tag along too?

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:33.770
Sure.

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:39.060
Nori, what have you been using for curtains?

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:44.900
I've been using ones I brought from home, but they're the wrong length.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.160
You're right.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.660
It's been bothering me since I moved in.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:57.660
Hey Yunocchi, get behind that curtain!

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.740
Why did you have to steal!?

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:14.140
Okay, it's 30cm. That plus the old ones is 180.

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:16.890
Thanks.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:21.100
Sorry it's so short. I got it at the hundred yen store.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:21.810
Don't worry.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.820
Yuno, hold still for a second.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.820
Wow, it worked on you!

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.790
Amazing!

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.980
It's this way.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:39.160
I'm already lost.

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:49.840
Miya, Sae's at the art shop. She wants to know if you need anything.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.890
I'm fine.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.320
How about you, Nori?

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:58.220
I'm fine for now, but where is it?

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:01.410
It's in the big department store in the next town over.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:02.850
Nazuna, do you know where it is?

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:06.440
Yes, but I've never been inside.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:10.110
It's such a big art shop.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.650
I'd like to go see.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:16.990
I had a class with Miss Yoshinoya today.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.040
Was it your first time?

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:23.750
Yeah. She said she'd model for us to sketch.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:27.500
"And if you'd like, I can model nude!" Right?

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:31.070
How'd you know?

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:33.380
That's just how she is.

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:36.930
Did she dress up?

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:41.430
Yeah, she changed into something frilly.

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:44.440
But then the Principal caught her.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.980
Sounds like it was pretty rough.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.020
There you are!

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.560
How long were you going to hide there?

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:30.520
I'm sorry.

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.540
This is I'm Home.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.290
I'm Home

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:54.090
That must be Townie!

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:55.550
It's not a real person.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:06.690
I know I could make something out of these!

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:10.650
Something?

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.070
Something!

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.270
Helmets!

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:27.030
It's fun looking at specialized stuff like this.

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:28.960
Impressive, I'm Home!

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:34.890
They have all sorts of towels.

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:36.810
Maybe I should do some shopping too.

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:39.340
Yeah, I'd like a small towel.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:45.180
Wow, is this a chainsaw?

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.900
It's pretty big.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:48.940
Pretty cool, huh, Miya—

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.440
A lumberjack!?

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.440
Necessities

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.440
Gen. Mdse.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.940
Stationery

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.280
They have lots of pens too.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:03.490
We keep getting distracted.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.790
Sorry.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.250
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.040
Me too.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:13.040
We'll wait for you here.

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.950
Go ahead.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:27.470
What do I do? It's gotten so quiet.

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:30.600
I'm the oldest one. I have to do something.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:36.360
Um... Um... I know. This always works in girls' comics.

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:44.240
Hey, Norippe...

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.240
Pe?

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:48.700
What color curtains are you going to get? Blue again?

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:55.030
Nah, I always get blue ones. I'd like something different this time.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:59.010
Wait, did I tell you blue was my favorite color?

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.180
You just have plenty of blue things.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.930
You're such a strange person.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:16.830
We haven't even made it to the curtains yet.

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:19.440
You end up wanting everything.

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:22.320
Here, Nori, use this.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:23.550
Thanks.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.540
You've picked up a lot too. What are you getting?

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:35.170
Um, some mineral water, lip cream, fabric softener, scotch tape,

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.290
and a towel and some batteries.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:40.920
Can't you buy those anywhere?

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.430
Here's the curtains!

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:51.560
Great, they've got plenty of different kinds!

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:55.150
Are you getting lace curtains?

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.560
No, just normal ones for now.

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:03.570
Look Yunocchi, I'm a lace queen!

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:06.820
Miya, you look like a bride.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:10.420
Do you?

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:12.240
I do!

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:21.710
Hey Nazuna, which ones do you like?

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:29.220
Maybe you should ask Yuno and Miyako instead.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:34.850
I'm not studying art, and I don't have any design sense.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:41.110
Why are you looking at it so one-sidedly?

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:47.910
It's not like we have good sense just because we're studying art.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:51.330
We're studying art because we think we don't!

00:12:53.950 --> 00:13:00.340
Sense is something you have to polish. You can't just say you have it or you don't.

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:13.100
I... I...

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:19.850
If it was for me, I might get these.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:27.200
They're cute. I'll get them.

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:29.110
But...

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:31.370
Yeah, I'm sure.

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:35.380
They've made up their minds, Detective!

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:38.370
Hey, stop staring!

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:47.590
Isn't that the landlady?

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:51.090
Yo!

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:53.170
Hi!

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:55.180
You're shopping too?

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:59.190
Yeah, I was thinking of planting something.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:13:59.940
Medium Tomatoes

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:00.690
Brussels Sprouts  Early Sprouting

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:01.440
Strawberries

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:02.190
Eggplants
Shimoda Eggplants

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:08.450
Hey, there's a garden at Hidamari Apartments, isn't there?

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:10.700
Why don't we all plant something?

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:14.200
Gardening is fun!

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.990
Gardening?

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:18.680
You mean like veggies?

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:20.710
Another kind of snack!

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.900
We'll do it!

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:27.520
Should we be deciding that quick?

00:14:27.520 --> 00:14:29.420
It sounds like hard work.

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:31.970
Yeah. Should we?

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:34.970
Let's all pitch in!

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:38.320
Why don't we? It'll be nice.

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:38.930
Okay!

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:42.560
All right! If you're going to, there should be enough for me.

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:49.320
I hope you can harvest a lot. I'll be looking forward to it!

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:00.160
Done!

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:03.170
Thanks.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.420
Norisuke!

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.480
Uh, me?

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:10.670
Can I have your old curtains?

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:14.640
Sure, go ahead. What are you going to do with them?

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.790
I don't have any curtains.

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:20.100
What have you been using for the past year!?

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:23.080
Miya has blinds in her room.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:23.860
Yeah.

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:26.110
Oh, that's what you meant.

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:29.110
But they don't come down anymore, do they?

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:32.490
Yeah, they broke last summer.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.240
Then what have you been doing!?

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:40.040
Knock it off, Hiro.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.120
It's Sae and Hiro.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:45.470
Welcome back.

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:47.050
We're home.

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:49.380
Oh, everyone's together.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:52.630
Hiro, what's in that big bag?

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:56.440
It's usually too expensive to buy,

00:15:56.440 --> 00:16:00.140
but the drug store at the station had it on sale really cheap today.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:04.140
Isn't
it
cute?

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:03.170
Isn't it cute?

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:05.690
Don't worry.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.440
Come on, Nazuna.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:10.700
Hiro must have bought it because she liked the pattern.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:14.610
I liked the pattern enough to buy it too!

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.660
You also bought these?

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:21.790
Tomato seedlings, huh?

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:27.030
I wanted eggplants and cucumbers too, but we voted for these.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:29.500
That's okay. Let's try growing these.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.000
All right!

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:39.010
Just tell me when you get tired, and I'll take over.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:51.170
Nazuna, can you help me with the watering?

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:52.520
Okay.

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:02.630
Here, Miya.

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:04.040
Thanks.

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:08.790
Here goes!

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:12.060
We're done!

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:18.020
Pizza! Neapolitan! Minestrone! Cacciatora!

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:19.760
You're sure in a hurry.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:29.170
Here.

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:30.470
Thank you.

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:32.020
Thanks.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:34.680
Why not turn the TV on?

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:36.280
I'll do the cooking.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:40.240
But we can cook.

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:45.090
Oh, you're not having any? I was going to make enough for everyone.

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:46.160
Thanks!

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:50.250
Hiro's cooking is so delicious.

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:51.780
But...

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.700
Don't worry about it.

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:58.420
Hiro, should we get another table?

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:00.680
Yeah, there are six of us now.

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:03.260
Should I get mine from my room?

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:05.520
Yunocchi, I'll help.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.040
Thanks.

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:13.400
We're off.

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:19.210
Excuse me!

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:22.530
Wow, look at this front hall!

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:25.330
I could fit my whole house in here!

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:32.330
Wow! Hiro, you really are good at cooking!

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:36.340
I wonder how it came out. Give it a try.

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:38.670
Let's eat!

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:43.860
It's good!

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:44.970
Isn't it?

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:48.470
Yeah, it's really tasty.

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:51.950
Go ahead, have as much as you want.

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:55.600
I have Hiro cook a lot.

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:57.620
She can cook anything.

00:18:57.620 --> 00:18:59.740
Oh, come on.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:06.200
I should've had Mom teach me how to make nikujaga.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.710
Hiro can teach you.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.210
If she lets me sample, I might join in.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:14.250
Settle down, Miyako.

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:17.500
You'll learn cooking recipe by recipe.

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:19.810
I was the same way.

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:21.220
Really?

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:26.040
I'm still not used to living alone.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:29.720
I'm having a hard time with school on top of everything.

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.480
It's okay!

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:37.610
Just take things at your own pace.

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:40.160
Oh, have you gone to the cafeteria?

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:41.490
Not yet.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:44.240
Want to eat there tomorrow, then?

